[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Audio Playback Test Specification
UID: YAAP-APTS
DATE: @GIT_COMMIT_DATETIME
PREFIX: APTS-

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @test_grammar

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Introduction

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document defines the test specification for Yet Another Audio Player 
(Yaap), a time accurate desktop audio player.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: File Handling

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: File Type Identification

[TEST]
UID: APLLSR-001-T01
TITLE: FLAC Format and Encoding Identification
TEST_TYPE: Functional
TEST_LEVEL: Integration
PRECONDITIONS: A valid FLAC audio file is available.
INPUTS: A valid FLAC audio stream.
PROCEDURE: >>>
1. Supply the FLAC audio stream to the audio identification subsystem.
2. Execute the identification procedure.
3. Examine the identified format and encoding.
<<<
EXPECTED_RESULT: >>>
The software identifies the stream's format as FLAC and its encoding as FLAC.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The test shall verify that the software correctly identifies the format and
encoding of a valid FLAC audio stream.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APLLSR-001
  ROLE: Verifies
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APLLSR-010
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST]
UID: APLLSR-001-T02
TITLE: Audio Track Identification
TEST_TYPE: Functional
TEST_LEVEL: Unit
PRECONDITIONS: An audio track with valid codec parameters is available.
INPUTS: >>>
Audio track information containing a track identifier and codec parameters.
<<<
PROCEDURE: >>>
1. Supply the audio track information to the classification extraction
procedure.
2. Execute the classification extraction procedure.
3. Examine the returned audio stream classification.
<<<
EXPECTED_RESULT: >>>
The software successfully extreacts the audio track's encoding and associates 
it with the supplied audio format.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The test shall verify that the software correctly extracts an audio track's 
format and encoding from its codec parameters.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APLLSR-001
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST]
UID: APLLSR-001-T03
TITLE: Multiple Audio Track Identification
TEST_TYPE: Functional
TEST_LEVEL: Integration
PRECONDITIONS: An audio file containing multiple audio tracks is available.
INPUTS: >>>
An audio stream containing multiple audio tracks with identifiable codec 
parameters.
<<<
PROCEDURE: >>>
1. Supply the audio stream to the audio identification subsystem.
2. Execute the identification procedure.
3. Examine the identified audio track.
<<<
EXPECTED_RESULT: >>>
The software identifies the first audio track in the input stream.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The test shall verify that the software correctly identifies the first audio 
track in an input audio stream.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APLLSR-001
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST]
UID: APLLSR-002-T01
TITLE: Supported Audio Format Detection
TEST_TYPE: Functional
TEST_LEVEL: Unit
PRECONDITIONS: A supported audio format is defined.
INPUTS: >>>
An audio stream classification containing a supported format.
<<<
PROCEDURE: >>>
1. Supply the audio stream classification to the format validation procedure.
2. Execute the format validation procedure.
3. Examine the validation result.
<<<
EXPECTED_RESULT: >>>
The software successfully validates the identified audio format as support.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The test shall verify that the software correctly detects a supported audio 
format.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APLLSR-002
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST]
UID: APLLSR-002-T02
TITLE: Supported Audio Encoding Detection
TEST_TYPE: Functional
TEST_LEVEL: Unit
PRECONDITIONS: A supported audio encoding is defined.
INPUTS: An audio stream classification containing a supported encoding.
PROCEDURE: >>>
1. Supply the audio stream classification to the encoding validation procedure.
2. Execute the encoding validation procedure.
3. Examine the validation result.
<<<
EXPECTED_RESULT: >>>
The software successfully validates the identified audio encoding as supported.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The test shall verify that the software correctly detects a supported audio
encoding.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APLLSR-002
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST]
UID: APLLSR-002-T03
TITLE: Supported Format and Encoding Combination Detection
TEST_TYPE: Functional
TEST_LEVEL: Unit
PRECONDITIONS: A supported audio format and encoding combination is defined.
INPUTS: >>>
An audio stream classification containing a supported format and encoding 
combination.
<<<
PROCEDURE: >>>
1. Supply the audio stream classification to the format and encoding validation procedure.
2. Execute the validation procedure.
3. Examine the validation result.
<<<
EXPECTED_RESULT: >>>
The software successfully validates the audio format and encoding combination
as supported.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The test shall verify that the software correctly detects a supported audio
format and encoding combination.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APLLSR-002
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST]
UID: APLLSR-002-T04
TITLE: Unsupported Format and Encoding Combination Detection
TEST_TYPE: Functional
TEST_LEVEL: Unit
PRECONDITIONS: >>>
An audio format and encoding combination that is not supported by the software 
is defined.
<<<
INPUTS: >>>
An audio stream classification containing a format and encoding combination 
that is individually supported but unsupported in combination.
<<<
PROCEDURE: >>>
1. Supply the audio stream classification to the format and encoding validation procedure.
2. Execute the validation procedure.
3. Examine the validation result.
<<<
EXPECTED_RESULT: >>>
The software identifies the format and encoding combination as unsupported
and returns an unsupported-encoding error.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The test shall verify that the software correctly detects an unsupported
audio format and encoding combination.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APLLSR-002
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST]
UID: APLLSR-003-T01
TITLE: Unsupported Format Error Generation
TEST_TYPE: Functional
TEST_LEVEL: Unit
PRECONDITIONS: An unsupported audio format is defined.
INPUTS: An audio stream classification containing an unsupported format.
PROCEDURE: >>>
1. Supply the audio stream classification to the format validation procedure.
2. Execute the format validation procedure.
3. Examine the returned error.
<<<
EXPECTED_RESULT: >>>
The software generates an unsupported-format error containing the identified
audio format.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The test shall verify that the software generates an unsupported-format error
when an identified audio format is unsupported.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APLLSR-003
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST]
UID: APLLSR-004-T01
TITLE: Unsupported Encoding Error Generation
TEST_TYPE: Functional
TEST_LEVEL: Unit
PRECONDITIONS: An unsupported audio encoding is defined.
INPUTS: An audio stream classification containing an unsupported encoding.
PROCEDURE: >>>
1. Supply the audio stream classification to the encoding validation procedure.
2. Execute the encoding validation procedure.
3. Examine the returned error.
<<<
EXPECTED_RESULT: >>>
The software generates an unsupported-encoding error containing the identified
audio encoding.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The test shall verify that the software generates an unsupported-encoding
error when an identified audio encoding is unsupported.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APLLSR-004
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST]
UID: APLLSR-005-T01
TITLE: Unknown Format Error Generation
TEST_TYPE: Robustness
TEST_LEVEL: Integration
PRECONDITIONS: An input containing unrecognised audio data is available.
INPUTS: An audio stream containing unrecognised audio data.
PROCEDURE: >>>
1. Supply the audio stream to the audio identification subsystem.
2. Execute the identification procedure.
3. Examine the returned error.
<<<
EXPECTED_RESULT: >>>
The software generates an unknown-format error.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The test shall verify that the software generates an unknown-format error
when it cannot identify the input audio stream's format.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APLLSR-005
  ROLE: Verifies

