[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Audio Stream Metadata Retrieval

[TEST]
UID: APLLSR-012-T01
TITLE: FLAC Channel Count Extraction
TEST_TYPE: Functional
TEST_LEVEL: Unit
PRECONDITIONS: >>>
A FLAC audio track with valid codec parameters and a defined channel layout is 
available.
<<<
INPUTS: >>>
FLAC audio track information containing a channel layout representing 
two channels.
<<<
PROCEDURE: >>>
1. Supply the FLAC audio track information to the audio metadata extraction
procedure 
2. Execute the audio metadata extraction procedure.
3. Examine the returned channel count.
<<<
EXPECTED_RESULT: >>>
The software successfully extracts the channel count and returns a value of
two.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The test shall verify that the software correctly extracts the channel count 
from FLAC audio stream metadata.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APLLSR-012
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST]
UID: APLLSR-013-T01
TITLE: FLAC Channel Count Too High Error Generation
TEST_TYPE: Robustness
TEST_LEVEL: Unit
PRECONDITIONS: >>>
Audio codec parameters containing a FLAC channel count higher than the permitted
range are available.
<<<
INPUTS: >>>
FLAC audio codec parameters containing a channel count that is too high.
<<<
PROCEDURE: >>>
1. Supply the FLAC audio codec parameters to the channel count validation
   procedure.
2. Execute the channel count validation procedure.
3. Examine the returned error.
<<<
EXPECTED_RESULT: >>>
The software generates an Invalid Channel Count Error.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The test shall verify that the software generates an Invalid Channel Count
Error when the channel count retrieved from a FLAC stream is higher than the
range permitted by the FLAC format.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APLLSR-013
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST]
UID: APLLSR-013-T02
TITLE: FLAC Channel Count Too Low Error Generation
TEST_TYPE: Robustness
TEST_LEVEL: Unit
PRECONDITIONS: >>>
Audio codec parameters containing a FLAC channel count lower than the permitted
range are available.
<<<
INPUTS: >>>
FLAC audio codec parameters containing a channel count that is too low.
<<<
PROCEDURE: >>>
1. Supply the FLAC audio codec parameters to the channel count validation
   procedure.
2. Execute the channel count validation procedure.
3. Examine the returned error.
<<<
EXPECTED_RESULT: >>>
The software generates an Invalid Channel Count Error.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The test shall verify that the software generates an Invalid Channel Count
Error when the channel count retrieved from a FLAC stream is lower than the
range permitted by the FLAC format.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APLLSR-013
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST]
UID: APLLSR-013-T03
TITLE: FLAC Channel Count Is Empty Error Generation
TEST_TYPE: Robustness
TEST_LEVEL: Unit
PRECONDITIONS: >>>
Audio codec parameters containing a FLAC channel count that is empty.
<<<
INPUTS: >>>
FLAC audio codec parameters containing a channel count that is empty.
<<<
PROCEDURE: >>>
1. Supply the FLAC audio codec parameters to the channel count validation
   procedure.
2. Execute the channel count validation procedure.
3. Examine the returned error.
<<<
EXPECTED_RESULT: >>>
The software generates an Invalid Channel Count Error.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The test shall verify that the software generates an Invalid Channel Count
Error when the channel count retrieved from a FLAC stream is empty.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APLLSR-013
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST]
UID: APLLSR-014-T01
TITLE: FLAC Sample Rate Extraction
TEST_TYPE: Functional
TEST_LEVEL: Unit
PRECONDITIONS: >>>
A FLAC audio track with valid codec parameters and a defined sample rate is 
available.
<<<
INPUTS: >>>
FLAC audio track information containing a sample rate of 44100 Hz.
<<<
PROCEDURE: >>>
1. Supply the FLAC audio track information to the audio metadata extraction
procedure 
2. Execute the audio metadata extraction procedure.
3. Examine the returned sample rate.
<<<
EXPECTED_RESULT: >>>
The software successfully extracts the channel count and returns a value of
two.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The test shall verify that the software correctly extracts the sample rate from 
FLAC audio stream metadata.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APLLSR-014
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST]
UID: APLLSR-016-T01
TITLE: FLAC Bits per Sample Extraction
TEST_TYPE: Functional
TEST_LEVEL: Unit
PRECONDITIONS: >>>
A FLAC audio track with valid codec parameters and a defined bits per sample is 
available.
<<<
INPUTS: >>>
FLAC audio track information containing a bits per sample value of 24.
<<<
PROCEDURE: >>>
1. Supply the FLAC audio track information to the audio metadata extraction
procedure 
2. Execute the audio metadata extraction procedure.
3. Examine the returned bits per sample.
<<<
EXPECTED_RESULT: >>>
The software successfully extracts the bits per sample value and returns a 
value of 24.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The test shall verify that the software correctly extracts the bits per sample 
from FLAC audio stream metadata.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APLLSR-016
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST]
UID: APLLSR-018-T01
TITLE: FLAC Sample Accurate Duration Calculation
TEST_TYPE: Functional
TEST_LEVEL: Unit
PRECONDITIONS: >>>
A FLAC audio track with a defined total sample frame count and sample rate is 
available.
<<<
INPUTS: >>>
FLAC audio track information containing 44100 sample frames and a sample rate 
of 44100Hz.
<<<
PROCEDURE: >>>
1. Supply the FLAC audio track information to the audio metadata extraction
procedure 
2. Execute the audio metadata extraction procedure.
3. Examine the returned duration.
<<<
EXPECTED_RESULT: >>>
The software successfully calculates the sample-based duration and returns a 
duration of one second.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The test shall verify that the software correctly calculates the duration of a 
FLAC audio stream using its total sample frame count and sample rate.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APLLSR-018
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST]
UID: APLLSR-018-T02
TITLE: FLAC Sample Accurate Duration Calculation Priority
TEST_TYPE: Functional
TEST_LEVEL: Unit
PRECONDITIONS: >>>
A FLAC audio track with a defined total sample frame count, sample rate, time 
base and tick count is available.
<<<
INPUTS: >>>
FLAC audio track information containing 44100 sample frames, a sample rate 
of 44100Hz, a time base of 1/1000 and a tick count of 5000.
<<<
PROCEDURE: >>>
1. Supply the FLAC audio track information to the audio metadata extraction
procedure 
2. Execute the audio metadata extraction procedure.
3. Examine the returned duration.
<<<
EXPECTED_RESULT: >>>
The software calculates the duration using the total sample frame count and 
sample rate and returns a duration of ten second.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The test shall verify that the software prioritises sample-based duration 
calculation over time-base-based duration calculation when both methods are 
available.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APLLSR-018
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST]
UID: APLLSR-019-T01
TITLE: FLAC Duration Calculation Using Time Base
TEST_TYPE: Functional
TEST_LEVEL: Unit
PRECONDITIONS: >>>
A FLAC audio track with a defined time base and tick count is available.
<<<
INPUTS: >>>
FLAC audio track information containing a time base of 1/1000 and a tick count 
of 5000.
<<<
PROCEDURE: >>>
1. Supply the FLAC audio track information to the audio metadata extraction
procedure 
2. Execute the audio metadata extraction procedure.
3. Examine the returned duration.
<<<
EXPECTED_RESULT: >>>
The software successfully calculates the duration using the time base and tick 
count and returns a duration of five second.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The test shall verify that the software correctly calculates the duration of a 
FLAC audio stream using its time base and tick count.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APLLSR-019
  ROLE: Verifies

[TEST]
UID: APLLSR-020-T01
TITLE: FLAC Unknown Duration Handling
TEST_TYPE: Functional
TEST_LEVEL: Unit
PRECONDITIONS: >>>
A FLAC audio track without sufficient information to calculate its duration is 
available.
<<<
INPUTS: >>>
FLAC audio track information without a total sample frame count, sample rate, 
time base or tick count.
<<<
PROCEDURE: >>>
1. Supply the FLAC audio track information to the audio metadata extraction 
procedure.
2. Execute the audio metadata extraction procedure.
3. Examine the returned duration.
<<<
EXPECTED_RESULT: >>>
The software indicates that the duration of the FLAC audio stream is unknown by 
returning None.
<<<
STATEMENT: >>>
The test shall verify that the software correctly indicates an unknown duration 
when neither sample-based nor time-base-based duration calculation is possible.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: APLLSR-020
  ROLE: Verifies

[[/SECTION]]

